Subject: [#94-5-76] filtering

A thought...
In the "scientific" community, it is common to submit any article complete
with a synopsis (abstract)...
This enables any other reader to quickly decide if there is reason to read
the whole article. Sometimes all the pertinent data can be gleaned from
the abstract and the article used without ever reading the whole thing! (I
personally don't recommend this...you'd better be damned sure of any info
you use in a professional manner...;-(
But the idea is valid, I think.
Unless your interest is completely static....any parameters you set would
need to be changed and updated periodically.
A filter that would give you a _short_ (repeat SHORT) abstract of any
articles in your selected categories (with capabilities of total recall at
your convenience) and inform you of all initial thread articles (maybe
even list all current threads with numbers and participants?[are you
listening, Ray?])...now this could be a useful filter....
Of course, the abstracts are the key....someone has to make them. They
need to be something more than keywords.....and something less than the
first 200 words.

Yes, Ray...I saw your post. I like the idea of 7 or 8 axes......just how
would the user rotate them, though?

Bo the Bohemian



